# A forgotten `|` between two operators on one line: DS0102, with a fix that inserts it.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 project customerId, amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..60
  PIPELINE@0..59
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..32
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..32
        NAME_REF@21..27
          IDENT@21..27 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
        GT@28..29 ">"
        WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
        LITERAL@30..32
          LONG@30..32 "10"
    WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
    PROJECT_OP@33..59
      IDENT@33..40 "project"
      WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@41..51
        NAME_REF@41..51
          IDENT@41..51 "customerId"
      COMMA@51..52 ","
      WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@53..59
        NAME_REF@53..59
          IDENT@53..59 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@59..60 "\n"

error[DS0102]: missing `|` before `project`
  --> query:1:34
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 project customerId, amount
  |                                  ^^^^^^^ `project` starts a new operator
  |
  = help: insert `|` to pipe into `project`: `| project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 | project customerId, amount
which parses without errors
